> > The grid argument can take a lot of different options, but with just an extent it isn't going to be fully specified, because the resolutions can still differ. I checked my code and, not being fully specified, the extents weren't being set exactly, so I fixed that on GitHub, but it's probably not what you wanted. You probably wanted to do something more like grid=list(extent=ee1,dr=500), for instance, if you wanted 500 meter resolution. The newer code on GitHub is also more memory efficient in that you can do something like grid=list(dr=500,align.to <http://align.to>.origin=TRUE), to calculate overlaps with smaller grids with cells that line up but the grids don't have to be all encompassing any longer.
> >
> > The extent() function on UD objects has confidence and coverage level arguments, because it's designed more for lining up plots, so those aren't going to necessarily going to return the same values. What you would want to check is the range of UD$r$x and UD$r$y, which are the grid coordinates, but with the newer code on GitHub only the resolution and offset needs to be the same.
> >
> > Best,
> > Chris
